Third-party code and attributions
================================

FlashInfer/b12x RoCE proxy
-------------------------
helios/native/roce_proxy.c was contributed by its original author from:
https://github.com/local-inference-lab/flashinfer/blob/f5f5341d711f8210ce91af5731a0841570f70e53/flashinfer/experimental/b12x/comm/roce/_roce_proxy.c
The proxy is compiled into Linux aarch64 builds. Its implementation is unchanged
from that revision; Flare adds a license and provenance preamble.
The upstream Apache-2.0 license is reproduced in helios/licenses/FlashInfer.txt
in the source tree and licenses/FlashInfer.txt in binary distributions.

libibverbs
----------
The RoCE proxy uses libibverbs and its inline header interfaces under the
OpenIB.org BSD license alternative. The verbs.h copyright and license notice
is retained in helios/licenses/libibverbs.txt in the source tree and
licenses/libibverbs.txt in binary distributions. The shared library itself
is supplied by the user's operating system.

vLLM
----
Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

ignition/components/markov_sampling.py adapts the sequential vocabulary-block
schedule from vLLM's DS41 fused Markov sampler:
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/df3bd094/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/amd/ops/fused_markov.py
Flare's implementation changes score rounding, explicit proposal probabilities,
and random-number domains for its probability-based rejection contract.
The upstream copyright notice is retained in that source file.

PyTorch
-------
helios/src/frontend/images/resize.rs adapts the resize coefficient generator
and uint8 antialiased convolution from PyTorch's UpSampleKernel.cpp:
https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/cf30153c4c131c8164ee7798e5022d810682e2cb/aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/UpSampleKernel.cpp
The scalar Rust implementation preserves adaptive coefficient precision and
intermediate uint8 rounding.

PyTorch's copyright notices and BSD-style license terms are reproduced in
helios/licenses/PyTorch.txt and heliopause/licenses/PyTorch.txt in the source
tree, and licenses/PyTorch.txt in the installed Flare package documentation.
The original copyright notices are also retained in the adapted source file.

